 - For a session that completes without error the hooks fire in the order `beforeSession` → `beforeUserInput` → `afterUserInput` → `beforeModelResponse` → `afterModelResponse` → `afterSession` ([validated by: fires the lifecycle hooks in documented order for a session that completes without error](../../src/config.test.ts#L132)).
 - A `beforeSession` that throws reaches the caller as a rejection, and also runs `onError` with the thrown error and then `afterSession`, because the call sits inside the same `try`/`finally` as the rest of the turn. An `afterSession` hook called under this condition can infer the session never advanced past `beforeSession`: no user-input hooks ran, no model response was generated, and no tool rounds were started — a cleanup hook that allocates in `beforeSession` and frees in `afterSession` will therefore always see the allocation and the release on the same error path ([validated by: runs onError then afterSession when it throws, and still rejects to the caller](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L116)).
 
+## Usage handed to afterModelResponse
+
+- The `usage` passed to `afterModelResponse` is the sum of every provider call in the turn, so a turn that ran two tool rounds reports the input, output and total tokens of all three calls rather than the last one alone ([validated by: reports 5300 input, 285 output and 5585 total tokens for a turn whose three provider calls reported 1240, 1835 and 2510](../../src/orchestration/turnUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L57)).
+- A round whose provider reports no usage adds nothing, so the rounds that did report are still counted, and a turn in which no round reported passes `undefined` rather than zeros or `NaN` ([validated by: counts the 1240 and 2510 rounds that reported when the middle round reports none, and reports nothing when no round did](../../src/orchestration/turnUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L63)).
+- The accumulation yields `undefined` when no round has reported usage — a turn with nothing to sum passes `undefined` rather than zeros ([validated by: returns undefined when both are undefined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L29)).
+- When the running total is `undefined` but the current round reports usage, the round's value becomes the total ([validated by: returns round when total is undefined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L33)).
+- When the current round reports no usage, the running total is passed through unchanged ([validated by: returns total when round is undefined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L38)).
+- When both the running total and the current round carry usage, each counter — input, output, and total tokens — is summed independently ([validated by: sums input, output and total tokens when both are defined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L43)).
+
